WEBVTT

00:12.512 --> 00:14.514
[poignant music playing]

00:25.108 --> 00:26.109
[exhales]

00:29.779 --> 00:30.780
[Do] Oh.

00:33.825 --> 00:35.201
[unbuckles seat belt]

00:40.040 --> 00:41.041
Mrs. Oh!

00:43.543 --> 00:45.628
- Are you all right?
- [groans weakly]

00:45.712 --> 00:47.922
It's absolutely freezing out here today.

00:48.006 --> 00:49.299
Do you think you can stand?

00:49.382 --> 00:51.134
- Yeah.
- Let's go.

00:51.760 --> 00:55.055
- I'm gonna take you home right now.
- Oh goodness, thank you so much.

00:55.555 --> 00:56.681
[Kyeong-suk groans]

00:58.266 --> 01:00.268
[poignant music continues]

01:11.863 --> 01:13.031
I'll grab that.

01:13.114 --> 01:14.282
There we go.

01:19.287 --> 01:20.413
I'm sorry.

01:20.955 --> 01:24.250
I guess now… I owe you another one.

01:24.334 --> 01:26.628
Don't forget to keep the promise you made.

01:26.711 --> 01:28.588
You said
you would take a break every hour.

01:28.671 --> 01:32.383
I know.
I try to do that, except it's not easy.

01:33.551 --> 01:36.888
I have to keep fighting for my son,
so that other--

01:36.971 --> 01:39.766
So that other people's
precious children are safe.

01:39.849 --> 01:41.601
Because nothing will ever change
in this world

01:41.684 --> 01:43.895
unless you do something about it.
Right, Mrs. Oh?

01:45.522 --> 01:47.065
I get it, I do. Except,

01:48.650 --> 01:50.985
your health should be
your first priority, okay?

01:51.069 --> 01:52.362
Goodness, Officer Lee.

01:52.445 --> 01:53.780
[poignant music continues]

01:53.863 --> 01:55.240
Thank you for your kind words.

01:55.740 --> 01:58.618
You might be the only person
in the world who cares about me.

01:58.701 --> 02:02.163
[chuckles] I'm just doing my job.
Go inside and rest up.

02:02.247 --> 02:03.081
All right.

02:03.665 --> 02:05.625
Oh, hold on. Just wait a minute.

02:05.708 --> 02:07.794
Just wait a moment. I'll be right back.

02:07.877 --> 02:08.795
Huh.

02:10.922 --> 02:12.048
[chuckles softly]

02:15.468 --> 02:18.471
- This is some kimchi that I just made.
- Oh.

02:18.555 --> 02:21.015
And it turned out really nicely. Take it!

02:21.099 --> 02:23.476
That's all right, Mrs. Oh.
I've got plenty of food at home.

02:23.560 --> 02:27.230
Come on, you said that you love
my homemade side dishes.

02:28.273 --> 02:30.483
- Mrs. Oh, that's really sweet, but--
- Please.

02:31.943 --> 02:32.861
It's just,

02:33.611 --> 02:35.363
when I see you, I think of my son,

02:35.446 --> 02:37.282
and it's… Please just take it.

02:37.365 --> 02:39.576
- [poignant music continues]
- [Kyeong-suk laughs]

02:41.369 --> 02:42.495
[Do] Thank you.

02:44.247 --> 02:45.290
Get some rest.

02:56.342 --> 02:58.344
[poignant music continues]

03:07.270 --> 03:08.938
[gun clicks, fires]

03:09.022 --> 03:10.899
[gunshot echoes]

03:10.982 --> 03:13.193
- [music fades]
- [Do] We're almost there, Mrs. Oh.

03:14.694 --> 03:17.488
Can you hear me? It's all gonna be okay,
but you need to stay awake.

03:17.572 --> 03:18.656
OPERATION ROOM

03:18.740 --> 03:19.866
Authorized personnel only.

03:19.949 --> 03:22.118
I'm afraid I'm gonna have to ask you
to wait outside.

03:29.834 --> 03:31.085
She'll be okay, right?

03:31.169 --> 03:32.170
[exhales forcefully]

03:32.670 --> 03:34.672
[uneasy music playing]

03:40.094 --> 03:42.805
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

03:42.889 --> 03:46.017
Where are you going?
Hey! Tell me where you're going!

03:55.235 --> 03:57.612
[tense music playing]

04:05.203 --> 04:06.871
That cop you hate just barged in.

04:11.417 --> 04:12.502
[man 1] What the hell?

04:13.503 --> 04:14.629
The pig is back.

04:17.423 --> 04:18.424
[sighs]

04:20.009 --> 04:21.594
I warned you, didn't I?

04:21.678 --> 04:25.640
Hey. Have you finally lost
your fucking mind or what?

04:27.350 --> 04:28.685
Where's Gong Seok-ho?

04:30.853 --> 04:33.439
[thumping, clattering]

04:33.523 --> 04:35.692
[men screaming, grunting]

04:35.775 --> 04:37.777
[thumping, clattering continues]

04:37.860 --> 04:40.321
[men continue screaming, grunting]

04:42.907 --> 04:44.701
[music fades]

04:48.913 --> 04:51.416
- [indistinct chatter]
- [patients groaning, moaning]

04:51.499 --> 04:53.251
[man] I said it fucking hurts, god dammit!

04:53.334 --> 04:55.712
- What's going on here?
- [phone buzzing]

04:55.795 --> 04:57.672
LEE DO

04:57.755 --> 04:58.756
[patient groaning]

04:58.840 --> 05:01.426
[Seo] Do, where are you?
What the hell's going on here?

05:01.509 --> 05:04.679
Pat down all the guys there.
See if anyone's got a list of addresses.

05:04.762 --> 05:05.972
Addresses?

05:06.055 --> 05:09.517
Guys, search all these lowlifes' pockets.
Hey, hold him down.

05:09.600 --> 05:11.561
Hold me down?
What the fuck do you mean, man?

05:11.644 --> 05:12.812
Stay still, shithead.

05:12.895 --> 05:15.523
Fuck you, asshole!
Don't touch me. Fuck off!

05:15.606 --> 05:18.484
[screams]

05:18.568 --> 05:21.029
Ah, you fucking assholes!

05:21.112 --> 05:23.573
Fuck! Ugh, damn it! [sobs]

05:23.656 --> 05:25.158
ORDER ADDRESS LIST

05:25.241 --> 05:26.075
[Seo] What's this?

05:26.784 --> 05:27.618
[Seo] Do!

05:28.119 --> 05:30.038
Did you check the vehicle
parked in that alley?

05:30.121 --> 05:31.831
There aren't
any security cameras over there,

05:31.914 --> 05:34.917
so I wanted to see if any of the cameras
around here caught anything.

05:35.001 --> 05:36.085
And the list?

05:39.505 --> 05:41.466
What exactly is this address list?

05:41.549 --> 05:43.551
[indistinct chatter]

05:51.726 --> 05:52.894
Compare these.

05:55.813 --> 05:59.525
- [Do sighs]
- "5 Domyeong-ro, 1-gil."

05:59.609 --> 06:00.943
Hey, that's Mrs. Oh.

06:01.027 --> 06:02.779
- [mysterious music playing]
- What is this?

06:03.613 --> 06:05.490
This is the same address as hers.

06:05.573 --> 06:06.824
That's right.

06:07.658 --> 06:10.912
I don't think all these recent shootings
have been happening randomly.

06:11.412 --> 06:12.580
What do you mean?

06:15.208 --> 06:16.542
It's been orchestrated.

06:16.626 --> 06:18.628
The guns were
couriered to all these people,

06:18.711 --> 06:21.547
so that means
that there's someone out there

06:21.631 --> 06:24.592
who's hoping
these desperate people will use the guns.

06:24.675 --> 06:26.427
[Seo] All of the suspects
in these shootings

06:26.511 --> 06:28.221
have been ordinary citizens.

06:28.304 --> 06:30.848
None of them have
sufficient wealth or jobs

06:30.932 --> 06:34.435
that give them easy access to guns
or any kind of illegal smuggling.

06:35.520 --> 06:37.438
I believe that these guns
were sent to them

06:37.522 --> 06:39.357
through an individual or group

06:39.440 --> 06:42.235
hoping to take advantage
of their desperate circumstances

06:42.318 --> 06:44.821
and their potential to pull the trigger.

06:44.904 --> 06:47.198
This list of addresses is the proof.

06:48.491 --> 06:51.828
So you're saying each box contained a gun
and a list of addresses.

06:51.911 --> 06:54.330
[mysterious music continues]

06:58.459 --> 07:00.503
Why would they put these lists
in the boxes?

07:00.586 --> 07:03.214
To expose each gun recipient
to each other,

07:03.297 --> 07:05.133
right down to their addresses,

07:05.216 --> 07:07.385
which would accelerate their anxiety.

07:08.010 --> 07:10.179
[Seo] Yes, the list shows
each gun recipient

07:10.263 --> 07:11.514
where they can find other guns,

07:11.597 --> 07:14.600
but also exposes all the other people
who've gotten them too.

07:15.476 --> 07:18.062
Yu Jeong-tae, the gosiwon shooter,
mentioned it, remember?

07:18.146 --> 07:20.523
[Jeong-tae] There are…
more guns out there.

07:21.274 --> 07:23.443
There are more people out there with guns.

07:24.193 --> 07:26.696
A recipient could come to your house
looking for a gun,

07:26.779 --> 07:28.406
and then if you decide you need more guns…

07:28.489 --> 07:30.116
You can go find them yourself.

07:30.199 --> 07:34.495
That's right. Jo U-tae saw this list
and came here looking for a gun.

07:35.621 --> 07:36.789
[U-tae] Evening, ma'am.

07:37.623 --> 07:39.000
Tell me where the gun is.

07:39.667 --> 07:41.961
And they're not just giving out the guns.

07:42.044 --> 07:43.963
They're probably surveilling everyone.

07:44.464 --> 07:46.340
Watching what each of them
will do with the guns.

07:46.924 --> 07:50.303
So do we have information
about the names on this list?

07:50.386 --> 07:51.554
[Seo] Look at this.

07:51.637 --> 07:54.682
When they first set up an account
for their cell, they create a username.

07:54.765 --> 07:56.309
I'm fairly certain those are the names.

07:56.392 --> 07:57.727
But this is personal information.

07:57.810 --> 08:00.229
How could they get their hands on
something like that?

08:00.313 --> 08:02.857
They probably installed malware
on each cell phone

08:02.940 --> 08:04.233
when the account was set up.

08:04.317 --> 08:05.318
Yes, that's right.

08:05.401 --> 08:08.654
We found malware set on all the phones
belonging to Yu Jeong-tae,

08:08.738 --> 08:10.615
Jeon Won-seong, and Oh Kyeong-suk.

08:10.698 --> 08:12.909
It kept track of everything,
including call history,

08:12.992 --> 08:15.036
text messages,
and all personal information.

08:15.119 --> 08:18.873
Hang on a second. Didn't everyone say
that the packages were delivered

08:18.956 --> 08:20.374
but there were no records?

08:21.083 --> 08:24.754
That's why I think that they deliberately
disguised them as packages.

08:26.214 --> 08:28.799
Having packages couriered is
part of everyday life for Koreans,

08:28.883 --> 08:31.302
and we don't notice
or interfere with other people's things.

08:31.385 --> 08:34.347
My God,
who the hell is behind all this bullshit?

08:34.430 --> 08:35.890
And what is it all for?

08:36.474 --> 08:38.643
If this is all true,
then we've got a huge problem.

08:38.726 --> 08:40.728
Let's start with checking the facts first.

08:41.312 --> 08:44.315
You'll have to figure out the legal names
of the people on this list

08:44.398 --> 08:46.025
and match them with each address.

08:46.108 --> 08:48.778
And more importantly,
you have to check if they have any guns,

08:48.861 --> 08:50.905
and if they do,
you'll confiscate them all.

08:50.988 --> 08:52.031
[all] Yes, sir

08:52.615 --> 08:53.783
Detective Seo.

08:53.866 --> 08:54.867
Yes?

08:57.870 --> 08:59.997
Lee Do was the one who found all this out?

09:00.081 --> 09:03.793
Yes, sir. Officer Lee found it out,
as well as the Oh Kyeong-suk incident.

09:04.377 --> 09:07.421
Tell him to be careful not to get into
any more trouble, since he's suspended.

09:07.505 --> 09:08.506
Yes, sir.

09:09.173 --> 09:11.467
However, it's also thanks to him
that we got this lead,

09:11.551 --> 09:12.885
so we'll have to work harder.

09:12.969 --> 09:14.428
- [Seo] Yes, sir.
- Get what I'm saying?

09:14.512 --> 09:15.888
Yes, I understand.

09:15.972 --> 09:17.974
- And tell him nice work.
- Yes, sir.

09:22.853 --> 09:24.814
[phone buzzing]

09:27.525 --> 09:30.069
Officer Lee?
Are you free to talk right now?

09:30.152 --> 09:32.363
- Yes, go ahead.
- [inhales sharply]

09:32.446 --> 09:34.782
It's about Moon Baek.
I went ahead and did some digging,

09:34.865 --> 09:38.661
and… Dongwol Industries is
a state-authorized arms distributor

09:38.744 --> 09:41.330
that exports weapons for military use.

09:41.414 --> 09:43.165
So they've got very strict security,

09:43.249 --> 09:45.876
and informed me they would
only respond to an official letter,

09:45.960 --> 09:48.421
so I looked for some basic information.

09:48.504 --> 09:49.547
[inhales sharply]

09:49.630 --> 09:53.509
Moon Baek had been working at the company
and quit right at the end of last year.

09:54.552 --> 09:57.388
And the reason that he gave
was that he had terminal cancer.

09:57.471 --> 10:00.224
Apparently, he was very popular
with his coworkers too.

10:00.725 --> 10:01.559
Oh, really?

10:01.642 --> 10:02.685
By the way, sir,

10:02.768 --> 10:05.229
how did you even end up
getting involved with that guy?

10:05.313 --> 10:06.439
Ah, well,

10:07.356 --> 10:09.358
that's a long story,
so let's keep it quiet for now.

10:09.442 --> 10:11.527
Oh, okay. No problem, Officer Lee.

10:14.155 --> 10:16.157
[groaning]

10:19.285 --> 10:20.745
[groaning]

10:22.622 --> 10:23.497
Hey!

10:23.581 --> 10:25.750
Where the hell did you go, huh?

10:26.250 --> 10:28.085
You're not supposed to just take off
like that!

10:31.297 --> 10:34.925
- Have you been here this whole time?
- Of course I have. Can't you tell?

10:37.470 --> 10:38.554
[Moon Baek sighs]

10:43.184 --> 10:46.103
None of this concerns you,
so why stick around?

10:50.358 --> 10:51.400
Well, this is

10:52.276 --> 10:53.527
a new side of you.

10:55.404 --> 10:57.114
You know, a "thank you" might be nice,

10:57.198 --> 10:58.949
if it's not too much trouble.

11:04.580 --> 11:05.831
[sighs wearily]

11:05.915 --> 11:07.625
I just can't figure you out.

11:13.172 --> 11:14.340
[Do sighs wearily]

11:16.759 --> 11:18.427
[Do] I should've called her back.

11:22.973 --> 11:23.974
What did…

11:26.936 --> 11:28.437
what did Mrs. Oh say earlier?

11:30.272 --> 11:31.148
[Moon Baek] Hmm?

11:33.359 --> 11:34.485
In the car, earlier.

11:35.236 --> 11:36.195
Wow.

11:36.904 --> 11:40.116
You picked up on that conversation,
even with all the chaos?

11:43.828 --> 11:44.662
She said,

11:46.580 --> 11:49.583
"At least now I'll die
without any regrets,

11:49.667 --> 11:53.045
so there's no need
for you to go to all this trouble for me."

11:53.129 --> 11:55.131
[gentle music playing]

11:57.049 --> 12:00.344
By the way,
why is she "Mother" in your phone

12:00.428 --> 12:01.512
if she isn't your real mom?

12:03.222 --> 12:04.181
Because…

12:06.600 --> 12:08.519
because she treats me like a son.

12:10.479 --> 12:11.564
Oh, right.

12:13.691 --> 12:16.152
Wouldn't your real mom be hurt
if she heard you say that?

12:20.656 --> 12:22.450
She died when I was young.

12:23.075 --> 12:25.369
- [sirens wailing]
- [officer 1] Stay still! Stay still!

12:25.870 --> 12:27.747
[officer 2] You are under arrest
for murder!

12:28.372 --> 12:30.374
[officer 2] You have
the right to an attorney!

12:30.458 --> 12:32.293
If you cannot afford an attorney…

12:35.963 --> 12:36.964
Sorry.

12:38.883 --> 12:41.677
I asked because I was curious,
since I don't have a mom either.

12:41.761 --> 12:43.763
[gentle music continues]

12:44.555 --> 12:45.973
You lost your mom too?

12:46.640 --> 12:49.393
I have no idea
whether she's dead or alive.

12:53.689 --> 12:55.191
The only thing I know…

12:56.609 --> 12:59.069
is that, apparently, it snowed a lot…

13:01.155 --> 13:02.698
the day I was abandoned.

13:04.116 --> 13:06.202
- [wind whistling]
- [baby cries]

13:06.285 --> 13:09.789
PLEASE WRITE DOWN THE CHILD'S NAME
AND DATE OF BIRTH

13:16.462 --> 13:18.464
[gentle music continues]

13:19.423 --> 13:20.716
[woman 1] Excuse me.

13:26.096 --> 13:27.932
Were you going to leave it there?

13:32.436 --> 13:34.396
Then you might as well hand him over.

13:34.480 --> 13:36.482
I'm the one
who collects the babies from there.

13:36.982 --> 13:37.983
[woman 2] Well…

13:38.651 --> 13:39.652
Don't worry.

13:40.778 --> 13:41.904
It's okay, really.

13:42.571 --> 13:46.075
It's so cold.
You shouldn't leave him there anyway.

13:48.619 --> 13:50.663
Does the baby have a name?

13:52.414 --> 13:53.332
A name?

13:55.251 --> 13:56.752
Before she abandoned me,

13:58.212 --> 13:59.839
did she even give me a name?

14:01.257 --> 14:03.259
[baby Moon Baek cries]

14:04.260 --> 14:06.262
[gentle music continues]

14:08.013 --> 14:10.015
[music turns unsettling]

14:14.270 --> 14:15.771
[man] Is it a boy or a girl?

14:15.855 --> 14:18.274
No idea. Let's go before someone sees.

14:21.277 --> 14:24.280
Well, hope it's a boy.
They're worth a hell of a lot more.

14:27.199 --> 14:29.201
[music fades]

14:31.954 --> 14:33.956
[upbeat pop music playing on stereo]

14:34.456 --> 14:35.708
FAMILY MILK DISTRIBUTION CENTER

14:35.791 --> 14:38.544
[man 1] Listen, if you're gonna buy one,
then why not just buy both?

14:38.627 --> 14:40.170
I mean, you could take just one eye,

14:40.254 --> 14:43.382
but then how the hell
am I supposed to sell a one-eyed freak?

14:43.465 --> 14:45.467
[man 2] Look, they said
they only needed one.

14:45.551 --> 14:47.011
And they also said they'd pay well.

14:47.094 --> 14:49.388
- What?
- They said they'd pay well!

14:49.471 --> 14:50.389
[music stops]

14:50.472 --> 14:51.849
What do you mean? How much exactly?

14:51.932 --> 14:54.184
Hundred million.
How does that sound to you?

14:54.268 --> 14:56.312
All right,
tell me what kind of blood type they want.

14:56.395 --> 14:57.521
Type AB.

14:57.605 --> 14:58.772
Ah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

14:58.856 --> 15:01.317
- Hey, hey, pick a fresh one, okay?
- Yeah, of course I will.

15:01.400 --> 15:05.446
All right,
let's hurry up and get this door open now!

15:05.529 --> 15:08.073
We're gonna make some money!

15:08.866 --> 15:10.618
Type AB…

15:10.701 --> 15:13.454
Let's see, let's see…

15:13.537 --> 15:15.873
Type AB…

15:18.500 --> 15:19.335
Hey!

15:20.294 --> 15:22.671
Yeah, you. Come over here.

15:23.172 --> 15:24.173
Yeah.

15:25.341 --> 15:27.343
[man 1 singing a happy tune]

15:28.886 --> 15:33.057
What are we gonna drink tonight? Soju?

15:33.140 --> 15:34.224
Oh, no.

15:34.308 --> 15:36.810
How about beer? Not beer either!

15:36.894 --> 15:41.148
Hard liquor, hard liquor!
We're gonna have some hard liquor!

15:41.231 --> 15:44.485
Let's drink that hard liquor,
yeah, yeah, yeah!

15:44.568 --> 15:46.236
- [man 1 sighs]
- [somber music playing]

15:46.320 --> 15:48.572
Good job. You got to keep one.

15:48.656 --> 15:49.990
[laughs]

15:50.074 --> 15:52.201
Hey! Let's go get some hard liquor!

15:52.284 --> 15:54.703
[man 1 singing a happy tune]

15:54.787 --> 15:57.039
[Moon Baek] At that moment,
I had a feeling

15:58.415 --> 16:02.002
that my life probably wasn't going to be
a walk in the park.

16:03.921 --> 16:07.883
And it turns out that feeling…
became my reality.

16:08.717 --> 16:10.427
[indistinct announcement over PA]

16:11.470 --> 16:15.265
After I got sent back several times,
by a few different families,

16:15.808 --> 16:17.935
they sent me somewhere really far away.

16:20.479 --> 16:21.563
[woman sighs]

16:23.107 --> 16:24.358
- Mommy?
- What?

16:25.025 --> 16:27.611
Tell me why it's good
that I'm going to the US.

16:27.695 --> 16:29.613
Anywhere else is better than here.

16:30.864 --> 16:32.032
Because of your eye,

16:33.117 --> 16:35.786
if you stay here,
you'll just end up in the gutter.

16:36.370 --> 16:38.539
The US is the land of opportunity,
you know.

16:39.289 --> 16:41.750
So try hard to make a life
for yourself there.

16:42.334 --> 16:46.088
And if you wanna be loved,
always keep a smile on your face.

16:46.171 --> 16:47.548
[somber music continues]

16:48.924 --> 16:52.344
One more thing.
I'm not your mom, so stop calling me that.

16:53.345 --> 16:54.388
It bothers me.

16:56.223 --> 16:59.852
If you wanna be loved, always smile.

17:02.813 --> 17:04.690
What a shitty thing to say to me.

17:05.441 --> 17:07.443
[dramatic music playing]

17:09.069 --> 17:11.697
- She said it was the land of opportunity…
- [door closes]

17:11.780 --> 17:14.116
- [child wails]
- [man 3] Hey, sit down!

17:14.199 --> 17:17.911
[Moon Baek] …but it was way worse
than any gutter. It was hell.

17:18.954 --> 17:20.998
[man 4] What do you wanna
get started with?

17:21.498 --> 17:23.500
Anything with a good price.

17:24.001 --> 17:24.960
Okay.

17:26.587 --> 17:28.088
[agent 1] Freeze! FBI!

17:28.672 --> 17:30.007
Put your gun down!

17:31.008 --> 17:32.468
[rapid gunfire]

17:35.512 --> 17:36.889
[agent 2] You, check over there.

17:37.514 --> 17:39.600
- [agent 3] Check upstairs!
- [agent 1] Shit.

17:39.683 --> 17:41.643
This kid's still alive.

17:41.727 --> 17:43.187
We need an ambulance here!

17:44.605 --> 17:45.856
[music fades]

17:48.609 --> 17:49.818
[inhales deeply]

17:50.944 --> 17:53.947
Unfortunately, I've got a great memory,

17:54.448 --> 17:56.450
so all that pain is still pretty raw.

18:00.412 --> 18:02.206
Now, don't pity me too much.

18:04.374 --> 18:05.375
Thanks for today.

18:06.335 --> 18:07.336
You should get some rest.

18:08.378 --> 18:09.379
That's okay.

18:10.672 --> 18:13.801
I may not have much time left,
but what I do have is loyalty.

18:14.551 --> 18:16.095
I'll wait here with you.

18:17.221 --> 18:18.597
[Moon Baek groans sleepily]

18:20.516 --> 18:23.268
[indistinct chatter]

18:29.525 --> 18:30.609
[Seong-jun] Fuck-gyu.

18:32.236 --> 18:33.362
Fuck-gyu…

18:37.491 --> 18:39.368
Don't ignore me, you little shit.

18:40.577 --> 18:42.579
You better be waiting
at the karaoke later.

18:44.748 --> 18:45.749
[Seong-jun grunts]

18:46.583 --> 18:48.168
[Seong-jun sighs]

18:48.252 --> 18:49.419
Why should I?

18:49.503 --> 18:50.420
What?

18:54.258 --> 18:56.760
[sighs] Why is this fucker
acting up again?

18:56.844 --> 18:58.554
I just don't wanna go.

19:00.806 --> 19:01.890
Say that to me again.

19:02.933 --> 19:03.851
Huh?

19:03.934 --> 19:05.227
- Don't wanna go?
- No.

19:06.395 --> 19:07.938
You listen to me, asshole.

19:09.022 --> 19:11.024
Want me to leak
those spycam pics you took?

19:11.108 --> 19:13.902
- [boy 1] Seong-jun…
- [man] Hey, you punks! Get to class!

19:13.986 --> 19:16.864
- [electronic melody playing over PA]
- Why aren't you two going in?

19:16.947 --> 19:18.574
The bell rang. Get to class.

19:21.660 --> 19:23.829
[teacher 1 exhales sharply] Little punks…

19:26.665 --> 19:28.750
- [Seong-jun] Hey. Get lost.
- [boy 2] Okay.

19:35.215 --> 19:36.175
[Seong-jun] Hey.

19:37.050 --> 19:38.051
Tell me that again.

19:39.052 --> 19:41.138
- You don't wanna?
- [Seong-jun kicks chair]

19:41.221 --> 19:42.264
You don't wanna?

19:43.056 --> 19:44.766
Answer me, you stupid bitch.

19:47.352 --> 19:48.228
Okay.

19:48.729 --> 19:49.646
Stop it.

19:50.314 --> 19:51.940
- [scoffs]
- [door opens]

19:52.816 --> 19:53.650
[door closes]

19:55.027 --> 19:56.403
Hello there, guys.

19:56.486 --> 19:58.030
[students] Hello.

19:59.489 --> 20:01.491
So what page are we on today?

20:01.575 --> 20:02.576
Stop it?

20:03.410 --> 20:04.536
[teacher 2] We're looking at…

20:04.620 --> 20:08.248
Hey. Since when do you think
you have a choice?

20:08.332 --> 20:11.335
You serve me.
and you should do as you're told.

20:15.964 --> 20:17.299
[inhales deeply]

20:19.051 --> 20:21.053
[menacing music playing]

20:22.763 --> 20:25.015
Call her "math whore."

20:27.768 --> 20:29.686
- No.
- Go on. Do it.

20:31.480 --> 20:32.439
Do it.

20:33.523 --> 20:34.733
Do it!

20:34.816 --> 20:36.818
I said do it, you motherfucker!

20:38.487 --> 20:40.072
- Do it.
- [fabric tears]

20:40.656 --> 20:42.241
- Do it.
- [music builds]

20:43.242 --> 20:44.701
[music fades]

20:45.410 --> 20:46.995
- What the hell?
- [teacher 2] Park Gyu-jin.

20:47.496 --> 20:49.706
- [exhales deeply]
- What is it? What's the matter?

20:52.376 --> 20:53.585
[Gyu-jin] Hey, asshole.

20:54.586 --> 20:55.587
Stop it.

20:57.089 --> 20:58.924
Just stop when I tell you to stop.

21:00.217 --> 21:01.927
I told you to stop it, didn't I?

21:03.136 --> 21:05.931
Just stop it. Stop it! Stop it!

21:06.014 --> 21:08.642
- [unsettling music playing]
- Fucking stop, you motherfucker! Stop!

21:08.725 --> 21:10.894
Stop it! Stop, you fucking jerk-off!

21:10.978 --> 21:13.063
Stop! Stop!

21:13.146 --> 21:15.148
[music fades]

21:20.028 --> 21:21.488
Fucking shit!

21:23.824 --> 21:26.576
Officer Lee is such a motherfucker.

21:28.662 --> 21:29.913
What do you think this is about?

21:29.997 --> 21:31.623
That's what I've been wondering.

21:33.875 --> 21:36.503
Who the hell is this fucker,
and why's that cop on my ass about him?

21:36.586 --> 21:38.588
[uneasy music playing]

21:42.092 --> 21:42.926
This is…

21:44.469 --> 21:46.596
What? Do you know this guy?

21:46.680 --> 21:48.223
He's one of Gu Jeong-man's guys.

21:48.307 --> 21:49.224
What?

21:50.225 --> 21:51.059
You sure about that?

21:51.143 --> 21:52.644
The day we took care of Mr. Kim,

21:52.728 --> 21:55.272
that guy was standing right behind him.
That's why I recognize him.

21:55.355 --> 21:57.524
No! This is wrong, you fucking animals!

21:57.607 --> 21:59.443
Damn you! I curse you, you son of a bitch!

21:59.526 --> 22:01.486
- [Kim screaming, yelling]
- Come on!

22:06.074 --> 22:07.534
[uneasy music continues]

22:08.535 --> 22:09.661
[exhales sharply]

22:11.330 --> 22:13.790
Gu Jeong-man. That shitstain…

22:14.583 --> 22:17.336
[Se-yeong] Dad, do you think
you could help me out a little bit?

22:18.086 --> 22:20.088
Hmm? Why?

22:20.797 --> 22:22.758
Are you in trouble? What happened now?

22:23.759 --> 22:25.510
[Se-yeong] Could I borrow
some money from you?

22:25.594 --> 22:27.304
[Cho] Why?
What are you going to use it for?

22:27.387 --> 22:29.806
[Se-yeong] I promise I'll pay you back.

22:29.890 --> 22:32.309
[Jeong-u] What's been going on
with Sergeant Cho lately?

22:32.392 --> 22:34.853
[officer] Someday, when you have kids,
you'll understand.

22:35.562 --> 22:39.024
Hey, look, just play dumb
until he brings it up himself.

22:39.566 --> 22:40.400
Yeah.

22:41.193 --> 22:42.736
[Jeong-u] I was just a bit worried.

22:42.819 --> 22:44.821
[officer] Oh boy.
They really are fighting.

22:44.905 --> 22:46.615
I don't see why
you wanna live in that place.

22:47.449 --> 22:49.618
[man] Are you
Mrs. Oh Kyeong-suk's emergency contact?

22:52.412 --> 22:56.458
First of all, the surgery went very well,
so there's no need to worry about that.

22:57.042 --> 22:58.752
Could you and I talk for a moment?

22:59.378 --> 23:01.380
[monitor beeping]

23:03.757 --> 23:06.885
During the procedure, we noticed
an infection in her internal organs.

23:06.968 --> 23:11.056
After the surgery, we decided to place her
in a negative-pressure isolation room.

23:11.556 --> 23:12.974
But, given her test results…

23:13.058 --> 23:16.061
[whispering] Thank you so much,
Oh Kyeong-suk.

23:16.144 --> 23:18.522
[doctor] We'll need to monitor
the infection for a few days.

23:20.649 --> 23:23.402
[woman on TV] Earlier this afternoon,
an incident occurred in the subway

23:23.485 --> 23:27.030
when a peddler selling toy guns
frightened passengers on the train.

23:27.114 --> 23:29.491
While trying to flee,
a mad crush resulted in many injuries

23:29.574 --> 23:31.034
as people fell on each other.

23:31.118 --> 23:34.079
Due to the series of recent shootings
all over the city,

23:34.162 --> 23:37.207
passengers mistook the toy guns
for real weapons,

23:37.290 --> 23:39.918
resulting in mass chaos
inside the subway train.

23:40.001 --> 23:43.338
Funny how the world can change
in an instant, isn't it?

23:43.422 --> 23:44.423
[Do] Mm.

23:45.090 --> 23:47.050
That's how scary guns are.

23:48.468 --> 23:49.386
Scary?

23:50.303 --> 23:51.263
Mm-hmm.

23:53.849 --> 23:55.142
Guns are scary.

23:55.892 --> 23:57.185
[pensive music playing]

23:57.269 --> 24:00.021
A long time ago,
there was a very peaceful village.

24:00.981 --> 24:04.443
And then one day, a man left a gun
at the town square and vanished.

24:05.777 --> 24:08.196
And then pretty soon,
that gun disappeared,

24:09.030 --> 24:11.825
and the town began to change drastically.

24:12.576 --> 24:15.704
As more and more people
were getting shot and killed,

24:16.830 --> 24:19.875
the villagers got
more and more suspicious of each other,

24:20.834 --> 24:22.461
and they all lined up,

24:23.503 --> 24:25.714
because they wanted to buy their own guns.

24:29.801 --> 24:31.803
And the man who was watching it all…

24:34.848 --> 24:36.683
smiled with satisfaction.

24:36.766 --> 24:38.768
[pensive music continues]

24:39.603 --> 24:41.146
Why do you think that he smiled?

24:44.316 --> 24:47.152
Well, maybe things turned out
the way he wanted.

24:48.153 --> 24:50.238
He made people believe
that guns equal justice,

24:50.322 --> 24:52.115
so they would rely on their power.

24:57.037 --> 24:59.456
- But what about all those people?
- Hmm?

25:01.082 --> 25:03.210
All the people who are getting those guns.

25:04.753 --> 25:05.754
Maybe to all of them,

25:05.837 --> 25:08.840
a gun actually could equal justice
and power.

25:09.674 --> 25:11.760
A gun doesn't offer justice.

25:11.843 --> 25:13.136
It doesn't offer power.

25:13.970 --> 25:16.264
Guns only bring you self-destruction.

25:17.349 --> 25:18.558
[music fades]

25:18.642 --> 25:21.394
That's why I think
you should stop looking for them too.

25:22.145 --> 25:23.897
If you don't have that much time,

25:24.648 --> 25:26.566
shouldn't you spend it on yourself?

25:28.276 --> 25:29.402
[exhales]

25:33.823 --> 25:35.450
By the way, who was that guy?

25:39.371 --> 25:40.664
The man who left the first gun.

25:43.708 --> 25:45.418
An Asian man with blue eyes.

25:46.169 --> 25:47.379
Least that's what I heard.

25:51.758 --> 25:53.760
[distant siren wailing]

25:55.762 --> 25:59.224
- [Jeong-man] All of them are in here?
- Yeah, I made sure to check.

26:00.850 --> 26:02.936
Jeong-man! Hey! You guys wait here.

26:04.104 --> 26:05.188
Ah, damn it!

26:09.526 --> 26:10.777
[bell chimes]

26:10.860 --> 26:12.946
[indistinct announcement echoing faintly]

26:13.446 --> 26:16.825
[man] Shit! When did they all get here?
Damn it.

26:16.908 --> 26:18.285
Did they say how U-tae was?

26:18.368 --> 26:20.704
Uh, according to the nurses…

26:22.205 --> 26:25.166
[sighs] …he might end up
in a wheelchair forever.

26:26.293 --> 26:27.419
[Jeong-man grunts]

26:27.502 --> 26:28.587
[Jeong-man] Fuck!

26:29.588 --> 26:31.673
[sighs] I told him
not to be so fuckin' rash!

26:31.756 --> 26:32.882
[exhales sharply]

26:34.509 --> 26:35.802
What about that fucker?

26:36.678 --> 26:40.015
The fucking cop who did this to Woo-tae.
Did you find him?

26:40.098 --> 26:42.475
No, not yet. We're still looking for him.

26:42.559 --> 26:45.228
Fuck! We just have to wait
and see what happens.

26:50.275 --> 26:52.444
So there's no chance
of getting better with surgery?

26:52.944 --> 26:54.279
[Moon Baek] I don't wanna do it.

26:56.448 --> 26:58.700
I don't need any more pain in this life.

27:02.579 --> 27:03.622
[exhales]

27:03.705 --> 27:06.041
[sighs deeply] Oh shit…

27:07.917 --> 27:10.211
- [exhales sharply] Fucking son of a bitch.
- [elevator dings]

27:17.177 --> 27:18.094
Are you getting on?

27:18.178 --> 27:19.179
[Jeong-man] Oh.

27:19.888 --> 27:20.805
Oh, sorry.

27:24.559 --> 27:26.561
[tense music playing]

27:42.535 --> 27:44.162
[tense music continues]

27:44.245 --> 27:46.247
[phone buzzing]

27:47.999 --> 27:49.584
Yeah, hi, Officer Jang.

27:50.669 --> 27:52.587
I'm at the hospital. Yeah.

27:53.963 --> 27:55.048
I'm heading down now.

27:57.175 --> 27:58.259
I'll see you downstairs.

27:59.636 --> 28:01.554
No, I don't need anything, thanks.

28:02.222 --> 28:03.264
Yep, got it.

28:04.724 --> 28:05.934
Officer Lee,

28:06.017 --> 28:08.019
wanna grab food before we go?

28:08.728 --> 28:09.729
I'm starving.

28:10.772 --> 28:12.482
Yeah, let's do that.

28:15.026 --> 28:17.028
[phone buzzing]

28:17.946 --> 28:20.073
- Excuse me.
- Yeah?

28:20.782 --> 28:22.534
- Something's buzzing on you.
- [music fades]

28:24.786 --> 28:25.954
I think it's your phone.

28:26.037 --> 28:27.205
[buzzing continues]

28:28.164 --> 28:29.165
Sorry about that.

28:30.917 --> 28:33.294
SEOK-HO

29:03.283 --> 29:05.243
- [Jeong-u] Hello, Officer Lee.
- Oh, you're here.

29:05.326 --> 29:07.579
This is Moon Baek. This is Officer Jang.

29:08.580 --> 29:10.290
Oh! Hello.

29:10.373 --> 29:11.833
- Okay, let's go.
- [Jeong-u] Sure.

29:12.751 --> 29:13.585
See ya!

29:14.627 --> 29:16.337
- You take care, now.
- Okay!

29:20.759 --> 29:21.968
Bye!

29:23.386 --> 29:24.804
[tense music playing]

29:30.226 --> 29:31.060
[engine starts]

29:42.822 --> 29:44.032
[man 1] That was pretty cool.

29:44.115 --> 29:46.993
[Jeong-man] Don't drive too close to them.
It'll be too obvious.

29:47.869 --> 29:49.788
[man 1] Hey, hey!
Mr. Gong is calling again.

29:49.871 --> 29:52.040
[Jeong-man] Fuck, why does this asshole
keep calling me?

29:52.123 --> 29:53.249
[phone buzzing]

29:53.333 --> 29:55.627
- Hey, why the hell isn't he picking up?
- I don't know.

29:55.710 --> 29:56.711
SEOK-HO

29:56.795 --> 29:58.963
Jeong-man, you sure
you should be ignoring him?

29:59.047 --> 30:00.215
[indistinct chatter]

30:00.298 --> 30:02.175
Won't Gong only become
more suspicious of you?

30:02.258 --> 30:04.052
[man 3] No.
He doesn't have to take that call.

30:04.135 --> 30:07.972
- Ah, shit. This is terrible timing.
- [man 2] Yeah, well it's not you.

30:08.056 --> 30:10.475
- [man 1] I'm just saying--
- Hey, you guys, shut up.

30:10.558 --> 30:11.476
[music fades]

30:13.978 --> 30:15.563
- Hello, sir.
- [Seok-ho] Fucking hell!

30:15.647 --> 30:17.524
You don't know how to answer
your phone anymore?

30:18.316 --> 30:19.901
Yeah, I'm sorry about that.

30:19.984 --> 30:22.195
A few of my boys got hurt
on the job tonight.

30:22.278 --> 30:24.489
- God damn it!
- So I've been a little preoccupied.

30:24.572 --> 30:26.491
- Listen.
- Yeah?

30:26.574 --> 30:27.742
Get over here now.

30:28.660 --> 30:29.494
What?

30:31.246 --> 30:33.414
- Right now?
- Yeah that's right, you fucking prick!

30:33.498 --> 30:35.375
Get your ass over here right away.

30:36.000 --> 30:37.043
Understood, sir.

30:39.838 --> 30:40.922
What should we do?

30:43.800 --> 30:44.717
Turn the car around.

31:08.157 --> 31:09.409
Bring them all in.

31:09.492 --> 31:10.410
[man] Yes, sir.

31:10.493 --> 31:12.495
[ominous music playing]

31:16.332 --> 31:18.251
[engine roars]

31:18.334 --> 31:20.336
[menacing music playing]

31:43.484 --> 31:45.486
[music subsides]

31:45.570 --> 31:47.864
[intriguing music playing]

31:47.947 --> 31:50.199
Explain. [sighs]

31:50.283 --> 31:52.869
[man 1] Looks like there's
a power struggle between the factions.

31:54.370 --> 31:56.122
I was reporting to some other guy
before you,

31:56.205 --> 31:58.541
collecting the guns
he was scattering around.

31:58.625 --> 32:00.627
[man 2] Things are more complicated
than we thought.

32:01.127 --> 32:03.838
If anyone catches wind of the operation,
it's over.

32:04.339 --> 32:06.507
We need to report to Jake
and pull out now.

32:07.133 --> 32:08.551
What about the guns? [sighs]

32:08.635 --> 32:11.137
[man 1] They're probably stashed
somewhere in Mr. Kim's club.

32:11.220 --> 32:14.182
But if we're taking over,
getting to them won't be easy.

32:15.266 --> 32:17.435
It's going to take some time
to secure them.

32:18.436 --> 32:20.229
[man 2] Should we revise the plan?

32:23.274 --> 32:24.275
Revise?

32:25.151 --> 32:26.069
For whom?

32:26.736 --> 32:29.197
[man 3] If someone else
messes with Kim's stock…

32:29.781 --> 32:32.784
Sir, things are looking
pretty bad out there.

32:33.409 --> 32:37.288
Bad news is spilling everywhere,
and also, Jake has expressed concern.

32:38.581 --> 32:40.959
Jake? What concern?

32:41.042 --> 32:43.503
Korea is heavily influenced
by public opinion,

32:43.586 --> 32:45.254
and if this rattles the plan,

32:45.755 --> 32:47.590
surveillance and regulations will only--

32:51.010 --> 32:51.844
Hey.

32:51.928 --> 32:53.930
[music turns uneasy]

32:56.432 --> 32:57.850
[inhales deeply]

32:58.810 --> 33:01.145
Of all the choices…

33:04.190 --> 33:05.441
who picked Kim?

33:06.693 --> 33:07.527
I…

33:07.610 --> 33:11.906
Ah, so… if there's a flaw in my plan,

33:12.824 --> 33:13.866
it's you.

33:18.413 --> 33:19.747
[Moon Baek sighs]

33:19.831 --> 33:20.665
Now,

33:22.458 --> 33:24.335
are there any more problems?

33:24.419 --> 33:25.420
[man 1] No, sir.

33:27.213 --> 33:28.506
Just give us the order.

33:29.632 --> 33:32.760
Look for anyone desperate enough
to get their hands on a gun.

33:33.386 --> 33:34.387
I will, sir.

33:36.556 --> 33:37.890
No more mistakes.

33:37.974 --> 33:38.850
[man 1] Yes, sir.

33:40.018 --> 33:42.020
[music fades]

33:42.103 --> 33:44.105
[uneasy music playing]

33:47.108 --> 33:48.484
Boss, the money's good.

33:49.152 --> 33:51.279
- Show them the merchandise.
- Yes, boss.

33:54.407 --> 33:56.617
- [man 2] I'm gonna show you something.
- [man 3] Let's see.

33:56.701 --> 33:59.328
- [man 2] Look at this.
- [man 3] Oh, that's sick, man.

33:59.412 --> 34:01.080
- [man 2] You like it?
- [man 3] Take a look.

34:01.164 --> 34:02.206
[man 2] One shot, one kill.

34:02.290 --> 34:04.042
[man 3] Wow, that's beautiful, man.

34:09.797 --> 34:11.132
[car door opens]

34:12.467 --> 34:15.720
Get your ass ready.
We hit as soon as the deal's done.

34:16.429 --> 34:18.473
Okay. Got it.

34:19.098 --> 34:19.932
Hi.

34:20.016 --> 34:22.018
What the fuck? Fuck!

34:22.101 --> 34:24.103
[suspenseful music playing]

34:24.812 --> 34:28.816
I didn't realize
that this fine pistol was only 250.

34:30.151 --> 34:31.486
Who the hell are you?

34:33.071 --> 34:35.948
It's a little sad…
that you don't remember.

34:36.032 --> 34:37.784
[surgeon]
What do you wanna get started with?

34:37.867 --> 34:39.118
Anything with a good price.

34:40.745 --> 34:43.748
- [man 3] What the fuck is going on?
- [dramatic music playing]

35:04.310 --> 35:06.687
[man 4] Boss!
Looks like there was an ambush.

35:08.022 --> 35:09.273
Dumb motherfuckers!

35:10.942 --> 35:11.943
[man 2] Boss, look.

35:13.820 --> 35:16.447
- [music fades]
- [breathing heavily, coughs]

35:17.323 --> 35:19.158
[ominous music playing]

35:22.078 --> 35:23.162
[boss] Damn, kid.

35:23.955 --> 35:25.206
You do all this yourself?

35:26.124 --> 35:28.126
[breathing heavily]

35:31.963 --> 35:33.673
[music fades]

35:33.756 --> 35:34.882
[groans]

35:35.716 --> 35:37.718
[breathing heavily]

35:40.888 --> 35:42.098
Finally awake.

35:42.932 --> 35:45.643
You know, you've been dead
to the world almost three weeks.

35:48.688 --> 35:49.814
Where am I?

35:51.107 --> 35:52.108
You're home.

35:55.236 --> 35:56.571
This is your home now.

36:00.074 --> 36:01.450
Are you a good guy?

36:01.534 --> 36:04.287
Good, bad… Depends on who you ask.

36:05.204 --> 36:06.539
But I can tell you this.

36:07.039 --> 36:10.293
I'm the best thing
that is ever gonna happen for you.

36:10.376 --> 36:11.210
Why?

36:12.336 --> 36:13.171
I like you.

36:13.254 --> 36:16.090
Yeah, but… why?

36:16.174 --> 36:18.134
You gotta look at it from my perspective.

36:18.217 --> 36:22.847
You see this little kid
with this cheap gun wrapped into his hand

36:22.930 --> 36:25.600
go charging headfirst into the lion's den.

36:26.184 --> 36:27.476
What is not to like?

36:29.312 --> 36:30.938
[groans, inhales deeply]

36:32.690 --> 36:33.983
My head hurts too much.

36:34.066 --> 36:36.944
Yeah, that's… that's a gift.

36:37.028 --> 36:38.946
It's gonna take some getting used to.

36:39.447 --> 36:40.364
A gift?

36:41.282 --> 36:42.408
I hope you like it.

36:44.577 --> 36:46.579
[brooding rock music playing]

36:49.123 --> 36:50.416
[object clatters]

36:53.419 --> 36:55.129
Welcome to the new world,

36:55.630 --> 36:56.839
Blue Brown.

36:57.715 --> 36:59.759
[teenage Baek]
What kind of people are you?

37:00.259 --> 37:01.093
[boss laughs]

37:01.594 --> 37:04.513
[boss] Well, anyone who wants a gun
comes to me.

37:05.765 --> 37:07.099
It's a tough business.

37:07.808 --> 37:09.727
That's why I need tough people.

37:10.811 --> 37:11.938
Like you.

37:12.021 --> 37:13.731
[teenage Baek] You chose the wrong one.

37:15.483 --> 37:16.776
I'm too weak.

37:18.152 --> 37:20.279
You're not the toughest kid on the block.

37:26.994 --> 37:28.704
But with this in your hand,

37:28.788 --> 37:31.123
you'll become a whole different person.

37:32.500 --> 37:34.502
[brooding rock music continues]

37:40.424 --> 37:41.425
From now on,

37:42.343 --> 37:44.262
you determine your own value.

38:01.946 --> 38:03.948
[brooding rock music continues]

38:14.500 --> 38:16.377
[Moon Baek] Bring up the gun locations.

38:19.797 --> 38:21.007
Start getting excited.

38:23.217 --> 38:25.720
Because a new world will soon be here.

38:32.977 --> 38:34.979
[brooding rock music continues]

39:46.801 --> 39:48.052
[music fades]

39:48.135 --> 39:50.137
[funky rock music playing]

42:18.244 --> 42:20.246
[music fades]
